# Sphere Waves — 2000 Fibonacci-sphere dots recorded into a Skia Picture every frame with wave-driven perspective and a hue-cycling gradient; tap right = new random "magic multiplier" (pushed to a history), tap left = step back in history; pinch changes the perspective distance and springs back on release.
# What this test covers: several right taps (new patterns), left taps walking back through the history and past its
# start (no-op), a right tap after going back (truncates the "future"), pinches in to 0.3 (closest the driver
# allows; distance x2) and out to 3 (distance x0.05, extreme perspective), a tap right after a pinch while the
# distance spring runs, and a rapid tap burst on both halves.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/sphere-waves"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 40000
wait 2000
# Forward through three new patterns.
press 300 437
wait 900
press 300 437
wait 900
press 300 437
wait 900
# Back through history and past the start.
press 100 437
wait 700
press 100 437
wait 700
press 100 437
wait 700
press 100 437
wait 700
# Forward again after going back (truncates the future).
press 300 437
wait 900
press 100 437
wait 900
# Pinch in, pinch out (extreme perspective), with the release spring.
gesture pinch 0.3 201 437
wait 1200
gesture pinch 0.5 201 437
wait 1200
gesture pinch 3 201 437
wait 300
press 300 437
wait 1200
gesture pinch 2 201 437
wait 1500
# Rapid taps on both halves.
press 300 437 --count 5 --interval-ms 100
press 100 437 --count 5 --interval-ms 100
wait 1500
wait "label=\"Close\"" 10000
press "label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
